      {
        "id": 228999,
        "name": "MindWanderer",
        "username": "MindWanderer",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/mindwanderer/{size}/4816_2.png",
        "created_at": "2020-03-05T19:58:12.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Beacon is definitely more Progress-y than Legacy, IMO, which is part of why she changes her name.&nbsp; If they split up, I definitely see Paul going with Preservation, especially in light of his becoming Heritage in the RPG.</p>\n<p>Tachyon is certainly the Chaos Lord, all right.</p>\n<p>I still see young Ra as Glory more than anything else.&nbsp; Maybe Progress (he's forward-thinking and hero-worshipped Legacy),&nbsp;but probably not now that he's Ra.</p>\n<p>AZ is probably Preservation.&nbsp; Bunker, too, though I can see a character arc that sends him toward Conquest.</p>\n<p>Not sure about Wraith.&nbsp; She's just kind of desparately treading water.&nbsp; She's fighting The Chairman and his Spites but she doesn't seem to have much of a plan beyond that.&nbsp; She doesn't want to \"preserve\" Rook City--it's never been a good place--but she doesn't have any ideas how to \"progress\" it, either.&nbsp; She's purely reactive.&nbsp; I can actually see Conquest being an option--she's moving openly and wants to \"win\" by brute force, really.</p>\n<p>Several of them would fight over Baron Blade.&nbsp; Clearly Conquest (he wants to rule), but also Glory (he wants recognition) and Progress (he wants to move toward a technocratic future).&nbsp; The idea of him being on the same team as Legacy is&nbsp;<em>delicious</em>.</p>\n<p>Citizen Dawn is similar--Conquest and&nbsp;Glory both suit her well, as does Chaos to a degree.</p>\n<p>Ambuscade has to be Chaos at this point.&nbsp; Another time, maybe Glory, but not now.</p>\n<p>Operative is Conquest here, for sure.</p>\n<p>Unity could fit on a few teams.&nbsp; Progress is a natural fit, but so is Glory.&nbsp; She is finally being recognized, after all.</p>\n<p>Visionary seems solidly Preservation to me.</p>\n<p>Proletariat doesn't seem to have any driving force in Mist Storm.&nbsp; Heck, in every story he's basically just obeying orders.&nbsp; Chaos would work better than anything else for him (and we don't have many other good Chaos candidates).</p>\n<p>Omnitron... doesn't really have a personality.&nbsp; It wants to progress&nbsp;<em>itself</em>&nbsp;but doesn't have any overarching ideals.&nbsp; It could be Conquest.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Now, all that said--even if there is a conversion kit, nothing says the heroes have to be on predetermined teams.&nbsp; They have to work mechanically, they don't necessarily have to fit into the story.&nbsp; And they could be alternate reality versions, not from Mist Storm.</p>",
